// font.kwxts — kwxTypeScript port of wxSamples/src/font/font.cpp
//
// The wxFont demo: a frame split horizontally into a font-attribute panel
// (FontPanel + FontCanvas, in fontpanel.kwxts) and a multi-line text control
// that previews the chosen font. Menus change the weight/style/size and load
// stock, system and private fonts.
//
// Run from the repository root:
//   bin\Release\kwxts.exe samples\font\font.kwxts
//
// Porting notes (details in the report):
//   * wxFontInfo is not bound. FontPanel::GetFontInfo() is expressed through
//     the legacy wxFont constructor plus the numeric setters, which produce
//     the same native font (see fontpanel.kwxts).
//   * wxFontEnumerator cannot be used: the native shim calls its virtual
//     callbacks through `int (*)(void*, void*)`, while kwxTypeScript's Callback
//     is a three-pointer `void` thunk. The return value that tells wxWidgets
//     whether to continue enumerating is therefore undefined, and no generated
//     accessor exposes the collected facenames. The "Enumerate ..." menu items
//     keep reporting the limitation.
//   * wxGetSingleChoiceIndex is bound, but its `const wxString*` argument must
//     point at a contiguous native wxString array. The binding only offers
//     wxArrayString::Item(), which returns a copy; there is no way to obtain
//     the array's element storage. The family and encoding choices therefore
//     use wxSingleChoiceDialog directly -- the same dialog wxGetSingleChoiceIndex
//     creates internally, with identical message, caption and choices.
//   * "View..." reads the message with wxTextFile and maps the charset with
//     wxFontMapper. The final step (wxFontEnumerator facename lookup) is
//     unavailable, so the encoding fallback font that the C++ code creates when
//     no facename is found is used there; wxEncodingConverter cannot copy bytes
//     for an arbitrary source encoding from JavaScript, so the text is left as
//     loaded (wxWidgets is Unicode internally and the old byte round-trip is a
//     no-op for printable text).
//   * Everything else, including the font dialog, private font, native font
//     descriptions, stock/system fonts and the character-table painting, is
//     implemented.

